  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> represents the current per division though the galvanometer.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7fd7a260-a858-45c5-8e33-e5c75a85aa26.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 93px;\"/></p><p>After applying shunt</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a915036c-8072-418e-80d0-5e9d20196de7.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 182px;\"/></p><p>Now, if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> is the galvanometer resistance, from the above figure, it can be written that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>24</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>24</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
